1292
00:56:46,337 --> 00:56:47,405
of our love for each other.

1293
00:56:47,405 --> 00:56:49,073
- [Mike] So I've hired Richard Crenna.

1294
00:56:49,073 --> 00:56:51,675
- Now the Reverend Snow
will be here in the morning.

1295
00:56:53,978 --> 00:56:55,313
- [Tom] You are a life saver.

1296
00:56:55,313 --> 00:56:57,615
I can't believe I ran out of holy water.

1297
00:56:59,950 --> 00:57:01,085
- It was in there.

1298
00:57:01,085 --> 00:57:02,653
- Okay, I'll climb in and you confess

1299
00:57:02,653 --> 00:57:03,688
through the little hole.

1300
00:57:03,688 --> 00:57:06,090
- Well, this much is real anyway.

1301
00:57:06,090 --> 00:57:06,925
Look here, Jenni.

1302
00:57:06,925 --> 00:57:08,425
- [Mike] A place to put your gum.

1303
00:57:08,425 --> 00:57:11,062
- You see, this is how
you gouged your hand.

1304
00:57:11,062 --> 00:57:12,697
You say you threw the skull down here

1305
00:57:12,697 --> 00:57:13,798
where Eric is looking.

1306
00:57:15,767 --> 00:57:17,202
- [Jenni] Yes.

1307
00:57:17,202 --> 00:57:18,870
- [Reverend Snow] Did
you find anything, Eric?

1308
00:57:18,870 --> 00:57:19,803
- Nothing yet.

1309
00:57:19,803 --> 00:57:22,440
- [Tom] Well I'll slap the
straight jacket on your wife.

1310
00:57:22,440 --> 00:57:24,042
- Surely, Jenni, you must agree with me

1311
00:57:24,042 --> 00:57:26,743
that anything as fragile as a skull

1312
00:57:26,743 --> 00:57:28,613
would have been smashed to bits down there

1313
00:57:28,613 --> 00:57:29,980
and Eric has found nothing

1314
00:57:31,048 --> 00:57:31,883
and to assume that the skull

1315
00:57:31,883 --> 00:57:34,452
could move on its own, all the way

1316
00:57:34,452 --> 00:57:36,053
from there to the driveway door.

1317
00:57:37,955 --> 00:57:39,323
Now Jenni, there's no reason for that.

1318
00:57:39,323 --> 00:57:40,825
- There's other skulls you can play with.

1319
00:57:40,825 --> 00:57:42,493
- Can't you see I agree with you?

1320
00:57:44,628 --> 00:57:47,332
Did Eric tell you I spent
over a year in a sanitarium?

1321
00:57:48,533 --> 00:57:50,902
- Eric told Ms. Snow that
you were very impressionable

1322
00:57:50,902 --> 00:57:52,103
but that's all.

1323
00:57:52,103 --> 00:57:53,303
- [Mike] You're actually nuts, huh?

1324
00:57:53,303 --> 00:57:54,872
- I know lots of people needing a rest

1325
00:57:54,872 --> 00:57:55,873
go to sanitariums.

1326
00:57:55,873 --> 00:57:57,675
- [Tom] Especially crazy people.

1327
00:57:57,675 --> 00:57:59,710
- This wasn't quite
that kind of sanitarium.

1328
00:57:59,710 --> 00:58:01,412
- [Mike] It was staffed by clowns.

1329
00:58:05,148 --> 00:58:09,320
- I grew up loving my
father and hating my mother.

1330
00:58:09,320 --> 00:58:10,455
Well she never knew it.

1331
00:58:11,655 --> 00:58:13,123
Something I kept to myself.

1332
00:58:14,992 --> 00:58:16,427
She was very beautiful.

1333
00:58:16,427 --> 00:58:17,495
- For an ugly person.

1334
00:58:17,495 --> 00:58:19,263
- Very gay like her.

1335
00:58:20,898 --> 00:58:21,732
Very much.

1336
00:58:22,833 --> 00:58:26,137
And I knew she resented that
I was not more like her.

1337
00:58:27,838 --> 00:58:31,575
I used to lie awake at
night, wish she were dead.

1338
00:58:31,575 --> 00:58:34,078
- [Mike] You know the gospel
speaks of losers like you.

1339
00:58:34,945 --> 00:58:37,215
- Well that isn't very unusual.

1340
00:58:37,215 --> 00:58:40,385
I understand many children
go through such a period.

1341
00:58:40,385 --> 00:58:41,852
- I was no longer a child.

1342
00:58:41,852 --> 00:58:43,555
- Oh, well it's hell for you then.

1343
00:58:46,357 --> 00:58:47,325
- [Jenni] One day--

1344
00:58:47,325 --> 00:58:50,127
- I stood by a chifferobe
and bored a priest to death.

1345
00:58:51,328 --> 00:58:52,330
- I got my wish.

1346
00:58:53,998 --> 00:58:55,165
They were both drowned.

1347
00:58:56,067 --> 00:58:58,535
- [Tom] I have to dry
clean my cassock don't I?

1348
00:58:58,535 --> 00:59:00,003
- I can still hear her scream.

1349
00:59:01,738 --> 00:59:03,340
I was all alone on a little beach

1350
00:59:04,942 --> 00:59:06,310
and all I could see
was the overturned boat

1351
00:59:06,310 --> 00:59:11,148
and the top of the waves and
I kept trying to reach them--

1352
00:59:11,148 --> 00:59:12,650
- As I held them under.

1353
00:59:12,650 --> 00:59:14,318
- The waves kept throwing me back.

1354
00:59:19,423 --> 00:59:21,892
- [Mike] Have you tried talking
to your minister about this?

1355
00:59:21,892 --> 00:59:23,093
- I could hear her cries no more.

1356
00:59:26,163 --> 00:59:29,867
Then hours later men came
and searched for the bodies.

1357
00:59:32,803 --> 00:59:33,905
They never found them.

1358
00:59:33,905 --> 00:59:35,840
- [Tom] Yeah, death's hard, ain't it?

1359
00:59:37,142 --> 00:59:38,375
- That's when this bad feeling started,

1360
00:59:38,375 --> 00:59:39,777
this feeling that if I'd really wanted to,

1361
00:59:39,777 --> 00:59:41,845
I could have saved them but I didn't.

1362
00:59:41,845 --> 00:59:44,248
- Well why didn't you?

1363
00:59:44,248 --> 00:59:46,317
- Did I really kill them?

1364
00:59:48,418 --> 00:59:49,753
- No, Jenni.

1365
00:59:49,753 --> 00:59:50,755
You tried.

1366
00:59:50,755 --> 00:59:52,757
You tried your very best.

1367
00:59:52,757 --> 00:59:54,492
- I didn't.

1368
00:59:54,492 --> 00:59:56,027
But (mumbling) begging and praying

1369
00:59:56,027 --> 00:59:57,395
couldn't make this feeling go away.

1370
00:59:57,395 --> 00:59:59,330
- [Mike] Look, what do you want from me?

1371
01:00:00,432 --> 01:00:01,898
- That's when they took
me to the hospital.

1372
01:00:01,898 --> 01:00:03,433
- [Tom] Well look, I got bingo.

1373
01:00:04,802 --> 01:00:06,137
- They told me I was cured.

1374
01:00:07,072 --> 01:00:07,905
- Jenni.

1375
01:00:07,905 --> 01:00:08,740
- Shut up.

1376
01:00:09,573 --> 01:00:11,208
- They told me I was cured.

1377
01:00:14,378 --> 01:00:16,647
(mumbling)

1378
01:00:18,348 --> 01:00:20,952
- [Mike] I found a screaming
hip bone if that helps.

1379
01:00:23,587 --> 01:00:24,422
- Mickey.

1380
01:00:24,422 --> 01:00:25,323
- [Tom] I'm rendering.

1381
01:00:27,725 --> 01:00:29,327
- Let's see, it's Tuesday.

1382
01:00:29,327 --> 01:00:31,262
Who was he stalking Tuesdays?

1383
01:00:33,497 --> 01:00:34,332
- Mickey!

1384
01:00:34,332 --> 01:00:36,200
- [Mike] It's time for
our discussion salon.

1385
01:00:40,103 --> 01:00:41,238
- You go on.

1386
01:00:41,238 --> 01:00:43,473
I'll be there in time for lunch.

1387
01:00:43,473 --> 01:00:44,942
- Where do you think
he's gone off to, Eric?

1388
01:00:44,942 --> 01:00:47,012
- Who knows about Mickey?

1389
01:00:47,012 --> 01:00:48,278
He might be hiding.

1390
01:00:48,278 --> 01:00:49,813
- You looked at Marion's grave?

1391
01:00:51,848 --> 01:00:52,817
- Nice wife.

1392
01:00:59,490 --> 01:01:02,027
- [Tom] Man my marriage
went down the crapper fast.

1393
01:01:06,730 --> 01:01:07,732
- [Mike] Yes, free!

1394
01:01:07,732 --> 01:01:10,200
I'm gonna strip down to
my shorts and watch golf.

1395
01:01:13,337 --> 01:01:15,540
- [Tom] Well let's see
how my poison ivy's doing.

1396
01:01:17,007 --> 01:01:19,577
(upbeat music)

1397
01:01:25,182 --> 01:01:29,353
- I think I'll slip down
to Cambodia for a minute.

1398
01:01:32,257 --> 01:01:34,258
- [Mike] Ah, I love my new jogging suit.

1399
01:01:36,027 --> 01:01:38,462
- [Tom] Saint Francis boxing pose.

1400
01:01:38,462 --> 01:01:39,997
Come on, come on.

1401
01:01:39,997 --> 01:01:40,832
- Mickey?

1402
01:01:40,832 --> 01:01:43,300
- She's buried underneath
a small changing tent.

1403
01:01:43,300 --> 01:01:44,135
- Mickey!

1404
01:01:48,238 --> 01:01:49,240
Mickey!

1405
01:01:49,240 --> 01:01:50,908
- [Tom] Mickey!

1406
01:01:50,908 --> 01:01:52,110
- [Eric] Mickey.

1407
01:01:52,110 --> 01:01:53,343
- [Tom] Having his own three legged race.

1408
01:01:53,343 --> 01:01:54,178
- Mickey.

1409
01:01:58,515 --> 01:02:00,150
Mickey!

1410
01:02:00,150 --> 01:02:01,785
- Ah, blow it out your ...

1411
01:02:03,955 --> 01:02:05,188
- [Tom] Come on, bring it
in, tough guy, come on.

1412
01:02:05,188 --> 01:02:06,723
Wait, in here.

1413
01:02:06,723 --> 01:02:07,558
Saint Francis.

1414
01:02:09,560 --> 01:02:11,228
- [Mike] Ah, so he checks Mickey's villa

1415
01:02:11,228 --> 01:02:12,663
in the south of France.

1416
01:02:16,300 --> 01:02:17,135
- Eric.

1417
01:02:17,135 --> 01:02:17,968
Did you find him?

1418
01:02:17,968 --> 01:02:19,137
- No.

1419
01:02:19,137 --> 01:02:19,970
Where's Jenni?

1420
01:02:19,970 --> 01:02:21,805
- She's with Ms. Snow on the patio.

1421
01:02:21,805 --> 01:02:23,107
Eric.

1422
01:02:23,107 --> 01:02:24,708
I think I should tell you
that Jenni's (mumbling)

1423
01:02:24,708 --> 01:02:26,143
me about the sanitarium.

1424
01:02:26,143 --> 01:02:27,245
- She (mumbling) you.

1425
01:02:28,578 --> 01:02:29,547
- Does your wife know?

1426
01:02:29,547 --> 01:02:31,082
- [Tom] We're not married.

1427
01:02:31,082 --> 01:02:34,552
- I told her Jenni was
impressionable but not (glitching).

1428
01:02:34,552 --> 01:02:35,487
Mr. Snow.

1429
01:02:35,487 --> 01:02:37,822
You can do both Jenni and me a great favor

1430
01:02:37,822 --> 01:02:40,057
by forgetting she ever told you that.

1431
01:02:40,057 --> 01:02:42,058
- [Reverend Snow] But
Eric, if it helps explain--

1432
01:02:42,058 --> 01:02:43,493
- It explains nothing.

1433
01:02:43,493 --> 01:02:46,463
- If I were you, Eric, I'd take her away.

1434
01:02:46,463 --> 01:02:47,632
If she's still impressionable

1435
01:02:47,632 --> 01:02:49,933
and that house frightens her so much,

1436
01:02:49,933 --> 01:02:51,568
why subject her to it?

1437
01:02:51,568 --> 01:02:53,303
- Look, I can't do a thing like that.

1438
01:02:53,303 --> 01:02:55,338
Be the worst thing for her.

1439
01:02:55,338 --> 01:02:58,877
Mr. Snow, it would be
admitting she was sick again.

1440
01:02:58,877 --> 01:03:00,043
I want her to be happy.

1441
01:03:00,043 --> 01:03:01,412
- [Mike] Mr. Slush.

1442
01:03:01,412 --> 01:03:02,613
- We'll stay here.

1443
01:03:02,613 --> 01:03:04,315
- Perhaps you know best, Eric.

1444
01:03:04,315 --> 01:03:07,785
- I've got a simple and old
fashioned piece of philosophy.

1445
01:03:07,785 --> 01:03:11,055
The only cure for her fear
is to teach her she's loved.

1446
01:03:11,055 --> 01:03:12,490
I mean really loved.

1447
01:03:12,490 --> 01:03:13,590
- I mean really, really.

1448
01:03:13,590 --> 01:03:15,125
- I love her so much.

1449
01:03:15,125 --> 01:03:17,027
- God bless you for that, Eric.

1450
01:03:17,027 --> 01:03:18,863
She's a very fortunate
woman having someone

1451
01:03:18,863 --> 01:03:20,297
like you to care for her.

1452
01:03:20,297 --> 01:03:21,898
- [Tom] But if you ever
need to swap wives,

1453
01:03:21,898 --> 01:03:23,300
just let me know.

1454
01:03:25,402 --> 01:03:27,172
- Be night soon.

1455
01:03:27,172 --> 01:03:28,973
- Oh Jenni, Jenni.

1456
01:03:28,973 --> 01:03:30,340
- [Mike] What, it'll be night soon.

1457
01:03:30,340 --> 01:03:32,108
(laughing)

1458
01:03:32,108 --> 01:03:33,810
- Darling, you've got to believe.

1459
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:36,347
It will not happen again ever.

1460
01:03:36,347 --> 01:03:38,348
- [Tom] Why did you call me Donna?

1461
01:03:38,348 --> 01:03:39,683
- [Eric] Mickey.

1462
01:03:40,885 --> 01:03:41,952
Mickey!

1463
01:03:41,952 --> 01:03:44,155
- [Jenni] Eric, Eric!

1464
01:03:44,155 --> 01:03:45,557
- [Tom] Don't touch Mickey.

1465
01:03:45,557 --> 01:03:46,823
You don't know where he's been.

1466
01:03:48,927 --> 01:03:51,562
- [Mike] Mickey's trying to
lead 'em away from his eggs.

1467
01:03:53,663 --> 01:03:55,933
(grunting)

1468
01:03:58,668 --> 01:03:59,570
- [Tom] You're it!

1469
01:04:00,938 --> 01:04:02,607
- What are you trying
to do with that skull?

1470
01:04:02,607 --> 01:04:03,673
- Stop it, it wasn't his fault!

1471
01:04:03,673 --> 01:04:05,342
- Where did you get it?
- Leave him alone!

1472
01:04:05,342 --> 01:04:06,177
- I'll take care of this, Jenni.

1473
01:04:06,177 --> 01:04:08,045
Now I know you don't like me, Mickey.

1474
01:04:08,045 --> 01:04:09,980
I know you've been wanting
to get us to leave here.

1475
01:04:09,980 --> 01:04:11,115
This idiotic attempt to scare us

1476
01:04:11,115 --> 01:04:12,883
as if we were children.

1477
01:04:12,883 --> 01:04:13,850
It was you, wasn't it?

1478
01:04:15,352 --> 01:04:16,187
Wasn't it?

1479
01:04:16,187 --> 01:04:17,555
- No, not me, not me!

1480
01:04:17,555 --> 01:04:19,357
- [Mike] And I dunno.

1481
01:04:19,357 --> 01:04:22,058
- Get out of here, get out of here!

1482
01:04:22,058 --> 01:04:24,562
- [Tom] Should I consider
that my employee review?

1483
01:04:26,663 --> 01:04:29,400
- [Mike] I'm gonna go back
and work for Leona Helmsley.

1484
01:04:31,635 --> 01:04:33,237
- I wish you'd apologize to him.

1485
01:04:34,438 --> 01:04:36,207
You know as well as I
do it's not his fault.

1486
01:04:36,207 --> 01:04:37,375
It's all in my own mind.

1487
01:04:37,375 --> 01:04:38,775
- Jenni.

1488
01:04:38,775 --> 01:04:39,777
- I've got your number.

1489
01:04:39,777 --> 01:04:42,012
- I'm gonna do something and
you're gonna help me do it.

1490
01:04:42,012 --> 01:04:43,080
- [Tom] Make canapes.

1491
01:04:43,080 --> 01:04:43,915
- What's that?

1492
01:04:43,915 --> 01:04:45,148
- That portrait upstairs.

1493
01:04:47,050 --> 01:04:48,652
It reminds you of your mother.

1494
01:04:48,652 --> 01:04:50,822
- [Mike] Chair made by Gateway Computers.

1495
01:04:50,822 --> 01:04:51,655
- Yes.

1496
01:04:52,790 --> 01:04:54,758
- You were fine until you saw it.

1497
01:04:55,727 --> 01:04:57,328
Now it has you all preoccupied

1498
01:04:57,328 --> 01:04:58,462
with memories of the past.

1499
01:04:58,462 --> 01:05:00,563
- [Tom] You're nuttier than a cheese log.

1500
01:05:00,563 --> 01:05:01,665
- We're gonna burn it.

1501
01:05:03,267 --> 01:05:04,102
- It's precious to you, Eric.

1502
01:05:04,102 --> 01:05:05,770
- The picture means nothing to me.

1503
01:05:06,937 --> 01:05:08,205
I want you to be happy.

1504
01:05:08,205 --> 01:05:09,707
- And dead.

1505
01:05:09,707 --> 01:05:12,810
- We can't be until this
fear is out of our lives.

1506
01:05:15,545 --> 01:05:16,980
- [Tom] Hi, I'm Hedda Hopper.

1507
01:05:19,983 --> 01:05:22,887
- [Mike] I'll just brush it
with a little olive oil first.

1508
01:05:24,055 --> 01:05:26,923
- See, we get this done, we've
got the day to chase Mickey.

1509
01:05:31,628 --> 01:05:33,297
- [Tom] Okay honey, now
lay against the painting

1510
01:05:33,297 --> 01:05:34,332
and light it.

1511
01:05:34,332 --> 01:05:35,165
- Alright Jenni.

1512
01:05:37,000 --> 01:05:37,835
Go on, Jenni.

1513
01:05:37,835 --> 01:05:38,970
- [Mike] Throw the M80.

1514
01:05:44,708 --> 01:05:46,343
- [Tom] If you imagine
it's a Leroy Neiman,

1515
01:05:46,343 --> 01:05:48,078
the scene plays a lot better.

1516
01:05:48,078 --> 01:05:49,480
- [Mike] Oh yeah.

1517
01:05:53,250 --> 01:05:54,418
- Please don't do this!

1518
01:05:54,418 --> 01:05:55,887
Hang me in a Comfort Inn!

1519
01:05:59,490 --> 01:06:01,558
(screaming)

1520
01:06:01,558 --> 01:06:03,995
- [Mike] Someone's radio
saw went through a nail.

1521
01:06:06,563 --> 01:06:07,932
- It's only the peacocks.

1522
01:06:07,932 --> 01:06:10,267
- [Tom] Yeah, their machining
some tools out back.

1523
01:06:16,140 --> 01:06:18,408
- And always, scary tuba music.

1524
01:06:24,648 --> 01:06:25,648
- [Tom] Hello.

1525
01:06:25,648 --> 01:06:27,217
- [Mike] Pepe Le Pew walked by.

1526
01:06:29,687 --> 01:06:30,755
- Fire's almost out.

1527
01:06:30,755 --> 01:06:33,290
- [Tom] Yeah, we'll have to
put you in to keep it going.

1528
01:06:33,290 --> 01:06:34,858
- Yes.

1529
01:06:34,858 --> 01:06:36,760
Can't let those ashes stand over night

1530
01:06:37,728 --> 01:06:39,397
and the brush in these
hills are a tinder box.

1531
01:06:39,397 --> 01:06:41,932
- So I'm going pole
vaulting is what I'm saying.

1532
01:06:41,932 --> 01:06:43,167
- [Eric] You wanna help me?

1533
01:06:44,635 --> 01:06:45,870
- [Mike] Oh, I've been waiting for you

1534
01:06:45,870 --> 01:06:47,838
to ask me to rake ashes with you.

1535
01:06:52,142 --> 01:06:52,977
- You feeling better?

1536
01:06:52,977 --> 01:06:54,878
- Ah, you read me like a book, honey.

1537
01:06:55,780 --> 01:06:58,015
- It's as if I destroyed
her with my own hands.

1538
01:06:58,015 --> 01:06:58,848
- [Tom] We'll have to advance

1539
01:06:58,848 --> 01:07:00,885
to my burning small animals therapy.

1540
01:07:00,885 --> 01:07:02,252
- She'll come back here.

1541
01:07:04,288 --> 01:07:05,522
She'll come back.

1542
01:07:05,522 --> 01:07:06,990
- Darling, if you go on talking that way,

1543
01:07:06,990 --> 01:07:08,458
you destroy the whole purpose.

1544
